@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Round 62 — Windows acceptance procedure (review branch)
+
+**Scope:** Windows workstreams 1–3. This is an **unexecuted** standard-user, offline test harness. It does not certify native Windows execution, IDE colours, shell, GUI Run or the installer. Workstreams 4–5 remain **not implemented**.
+
+## Run on a genuine Windows 10/11 desktop
+
+Use a **normal non-elevated 64-bit PowerShell 5.1+** session. Clone/check out this review branch, install NASM + MinGW PE64 linker/compiler using the machine's existing approved build environment (never elevate or weaken protection for this test). From the repo root:
+
+```powershell
+powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\tools\r62_windows_acceptance.ps1 -Stage Prepare
+# If a real pre-R61 executable is available, re-run Prepare with:
+#  -LegacyCompiler "C:\path\to\pre-r61\sutram.exe"
+```
+
+The Prepare stage calls `tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1`, requiring `R61_PE_NORMAL_SIZE` and `R61_WINDOWS_COMPILE_EXECUTE_PASS` from **real** native Windows stdout, with the 64 KiB runaway-output guard and 12 s bounded processes. The optional legacy A/B prints `legacy-compile` elapsed time, exit, and observed output size; record those numbers, do not infer them. After success, it rebuilds `win/sutram.exe`, `sutram-ide-gui.exe`, and `windows/native-installer/output/Sutram-Setup-0.1.0-native-x64.exe` with the **current compiler** embedded; runs package `--self-test`; checks canonical `icons/sutram.ico` SHA; and saves `build-manifest.txt` to `%TEMP%\Sutram-R62-Windows-Acceptance`.
+
+**Stop if Prepare fails.** Do not claim R61 fixed until the generated program really executes. With a passing Prepare, run the newly built setup EXE **interactively as standard user**, choose per-user `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Sutram`, complete the wizard, and note any failure text. No UAC should appear. If installation fails, retain `%TEMP%\Sutram-Setup-*\install.log`; report the actual `ERROR:` entry and do not infer a cause.
+
+Then:
+
+```powershell
+powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\tools\r62_windows_acceptance.ps1 -Stage Audit
+```
+
+Audit checks `HKCU\...\Uninstall\Sutram`, actual per-user install marker, real saved `install.log` and completion event, correct Start Menu `Sutram IDE.lnk` target and canonical ICO **byte hash**, byte equality of installed compiler with just-built compiler, bounded compilation of `R62_COLOUR_FIXTURE.sm`, actual generated PE stdout `R62_SHELL_AND_RUN_OK`, and creation of the installed GUI window. This is **not** an automated wizard-click test or evidence that visual colours/shell Run work.
+
+## GUI screenshot and manual acceptance
+
+In the installed GUI use **File > Open** to load `%TEMP%\Sutram-R62-Windows-Acceptance\R62_COLOUR_FIXTURE.sm`. Visually compare **orange keywords** (`mukhya`, `vitti`, `yadi`), **teal builtin** (`likha`), **green string**, **purple 123**, **grey # comment**. Check menus (File / Edit / Shell / Debug / Options / Window / Help), editor **Run** actual stdout, and `>>>` shell execution. If any fails, report the real symptom.
+
+With that actual fixture visible, capture the desktop:
+
+```powershell
+powershell.exe -NoProfile -File .\tools\r62_windows_acceptance.ps1 -Stage Screenshot -CaptureGui
+```
+
+This produces `GUI_REVIEW_REQUIRED.png` beside the logs. **Someone must actually open and visually inspect it.** Capture install wizard and Start Menu shortcut icon separately; an ICO file's hash alone is not visual confirmation. Do not assume a GitHub runner has an interactive desktop.
+
+## Preserved safety / limitations
+
+- `windows/native-installer/install-core.ps1` restores R61's **bounded 8-second pre/post compiler self-tests** that were absent from `main`, and copies the successful installation log into `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Sutram\install.log`. Failure leaves the wizard's temporary log for diagnosis.
+- `tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1` is restored from the existing R61 draft branch with its original content. No assertion of fresh Windows results.
+- `.github/workflows/r59-native.yml` removes an inherited `push` trigger; all repo workflows on **this branch** remain manual-only. No new workflows created, no CI runs launched, no notification flood.
+- **No** compiler, language pack, approved golden, or GUI source code changed. No network calls, secrets, UAC elevation, HKLM writes or bypasses introduced.
+- **Round 62 workstreams 4 and 5 remain open.** Push/pop and store/reload peephole need proven emission-site safety plus instruction counts and gates; automatic overflow traps need an opt-in compatibility story and actual native before/after evidence. Neither is claimed here.

diff --git a/tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1 b/tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,123 @@
+#requires -version 5.1
+# R61: staged native compiler fault localisation, run deliberately on real Windows.
+# Usage: powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools/r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1
+# Never elevate, disable UAC, or modify user security settings.
+[CmdletBinding()]
+param(
+    [string]$ResultsDir = "",
+    [int]$TimeoutMs = 8000,
+    [string]$NasmPath = "",
+    [string]$LinkerPath = "",
+    [string]$LegacyCompiler = ""
+)
+$ErrorActionPreference = 'Stop'
+$root = (Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')).Path
+if (-not $ResultsDir) { $ResultsDir = Join-Path $env:TEMP ('Sutram-R61-' + [guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')) }
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ResultsDir | Out-Null
+$ResultsDir = (Resolve-Path -LiteralPath $ResultsDir).Path
+if ($TimeoutMs -lt 1000 -or $TimeoutMs -gt 60000) { throw 'TimeoutMs must be 1000..60000.' }
+if (-not $NasmPath) {
+    $n = Get-Command nasm.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
+    if (-not $n) { $n = Get-Command nasm -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
+    if (-not $n) { throw 'A Windows NASM is required (nasm.exe in PATH or -NasmPath).' }
+    $NasmPath = $n.Source
+}
+if (-not $LinkerPath) {
+    $ld = Get-Command ld.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
+    if (-not $ld) { throw 'A MinGW PE64 linker is required (ld.exe in PATH or -LinkerPath).' }
+    $LinkerPath = $ld.Source
+}
+$srcAsm = Join-Path $root 'src\sutram_compiler.asm'
+$fixture = Join-Path $ResultsDir 'win_native_test.sm'
+[IO.File]::WriteAllText($fixture, ("mukhya() {" + [Environment]::NewLine + '    likha("WIN_NATIVE_TEST_OK")' + [Environment]::NewLine + "}" + [Environment]::NewLine), ([Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)))
+function Invoke-Bounded([string]$Path, [string]$Arguments, [string]$Tag, [string]$WatchOutput = "") {
+    $out = Join-Path $ResultsDir ($Tag + '.stdout.txt')
+    $err = Join-Path $ResultsDir ($Tag + '.stderr.txt')
+    $sw = [Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()
+    $startup = @{ FilePath=$Path; WorkingDirectory=$root; PassThru=$true; NoNewWindow=$true; RedirectStandardOutput=$out; RedirectStandardError=$err }
+    if ($Arguments) { $startup.ArgumentList = $Arguments }
+    $proc = Start-Process @startup
+    $timedOut = $false
+    $oversize = $false
+    try {
+        # Enforce size and wall-clock limits; the R60 native failure wrote
+        # more than 500 MB of zero padding in less than 12 seconds.
+        while (-not $proc.HasExited -and $sw.ElapsedMilliseconds -lt $TimeoutMs) {
+            if ($WatchOutput -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath $WatchOutput -PathType Leaf) -and
+                (Get-Item -LiteralPath $WatchOutput).Length -gt 65536) {
+                $oversize = $true
+                break
+            }
+            Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 80
+            $proc.Refresh()
+        }
+        if (-not $proc.HasExited) {
+            $timedOut = -not $oversize
+            Stop-Process -Id $proc.Id -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue
+            [void]$proc.WaitForExit(3000)
+        }
+        $code = if ($oversize) { -9998 } elseif ($timedOut) { -9999 } else { $proc.ExitCode }
+    } finally { $sw.Stop(); $proc.Dispose() }
+    $stdout = if(Test-Path $out) {[IO.File]::ReadAllText($out)} else {''}
+    $stderr = if(Test-Path $err) {[IO.File]::ReadAllText($err)} else {''}
+    Write-Host ("R61_STAGE tag={0} timeout={1} oversize={2} exit={3} ms={4} stdout={5} stderr={6}" -f $Tag,$timedOut,$oversize,$code,$sw.ElapsedMilliseconds,($stdout -replace "[\r\n]+"," | "),($stderr -replace "[\r\n]+"," | "))
+    if ($oversize) { Write-Host ("R61_PE_SIZE_REGRESSION bytes=" + (Get-Item -LiteralPath $WatchOutput).Length) }
+    return [pscustomobject]@{ Tag=$Tag; TimedOut=$timedOut; Oversize=$oversize; Exit=$code; Ms=$sw.ElapsedMilliseconds; Stdout=$stdout; Stderr=$stderr }
+}
+function Compile-Native([string]$Tag, [string]$ExtraDefine = '') {
+    $obj = Join-Path $ResultsDir ($Tag + '.obj')
+    $exe = Join-Path $ResultsDir ($Tag + '.exe')
+    $params = @('-f','win64','-dWINDOWS')
+    if ($ExtraDefine) { $params += $ExtraDefine }
+    $params += @('-I.',$srcAsm,'-o',$obj)
+    Push-Location $root
+    try {
+        & $NasmPath @params
+        if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "NASM failed for $Tag (exit $LASTEXITCODE)." }
+        & $LinkerPath -mi386pep --entry=_start -o $exe $obj
+        if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw "PE linker failed for $Tag (exit $LASTEXITCODE)." }
+    } finally { Pop-Location }
+    $header=[IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($exe)
+    if ($header.Length -lt 512 -or $header[0] -ne 77 -or $header[1] -ne 90) { throw "Not a PE file: $exe" }
+    Write-Host ("R61_BUILT tag={0} bytes={1} sha256={2}" -f $Tag, $header.Length, (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $exe -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant())
+    return $exe
+}
+Write-Host ("R61_ENVIRONMENT user={0} os={1} nasm={2} linker={3} workdir={4}" -f $env:USERNAME,[Environment]::OSVersion,$NasmPath,$LinkerPath,$ResultsDir)
+Write-Host ("R61_SOURCE_SHA256 compiler={0}" -f (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $srcAsm -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant())
+$reference = Compile-Native 'sutram-r61-fresh'
+if ($LegacyCompiler) {
+    if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $LegacyCompiler -PathType Leaf)) { throw 'Specified LegacyCompiler not found.' }
+    Write-Host ("R61_LEGACY_SHA256 "+(Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $LegacyCompiler -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant())
+    [void](Invoke-Bounded $LegacyCompiler '--version' 'legacy-version')
+    $oldOut = Join-Path $ResultsDir 'legacy_program.exe'
+    [void](Invoke-Bounded $LegacyCompiler ('"' + $fixture + '" "' + $oldOut + '"') 'legacy-compile' $oldOut)
+}
+# Probe instructions are already defined at compiler entry. No instrumentation
+# inside production code or mutation of any accepted codegen baseline.
+for ($i=0; $i -le 7; $i++) {
+    $probe = Compile-Native ("probe-" + $i) ("-DR49_WIN_DIAG_" + $i)
+    $out = Join-Path $ResultsDir ("probe-" + $i + '-program.exe')
+    [void](Invoke-Bounded $probe ('"' + $fixture + '" "' + $out + '"') ("probe-" + $i))
+}
+$ver = Invoke-Bounded $reference '--version' 'fresh-version'
+$help = Invoke-Bounded $reference '--help' 'fresh-help'
+$check = Invoke-Bounded $reference ('--check "' + $fixture + '"') 'fresh-check'
+$exe = Join-Path $ResultsDir 'fresh-program.exe'
+$compiled = Invoke-Bounded $reference ('"' + $fixture + '" "' + $exe + '"') 'fresh-compile' $exe
+$accepted = $false
+if (!$compiled.TimedOut -and !$compiled.Oversize -and $compiled.Exit -eq 0 -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath $exe -PathType Leaf)) {
+    Write-Host ("R61_PE_NORMAL_SIZE bytes=" + (Get-Item -LiteralPath $exe).Length)
+    if ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $exe).Length -gt 65536) { throw "R61 PE output unexpectedly exceeds 64 KiB" }
+    $prog = Invoke-Bounded $exe '' 'fresh-program'
+    if (!$prog.TimedOut -and !$prog.Oversize -and $prog.Exit -eq 0 -and $prog.Stdout.Trim() -eq 'WIN_NATIVE_TEST_OK') {
+        $accepted = $true
+        Write-Host 'R61_WINDOWS_COMPILE_EXECUTE_PASS'
+    } else {
+        Write-Host 'R61_WINDOWS_COMPILE_EXECUTE_FAIL: generated PE runtime failed'
+    }
+} else {
+    Write-Host 'R61_WINDOWS_COMPILE_EXECUTE_FAIL: compiler did not produce a program'
+}
+Write-Host "R61_DIAGNOSTICS_COMPLETE $ResultsDir"
+Write-Host 'Interpretation: probe 0/1/2 isolate bootstrap, probe 3 file read (exit=source byte length), probe 4 graph, 5 import expansion, 6 lexer, 7 parser. A completing probe does NOT prove downstream phases.'
+if (-not $accepted) { throw 'R61 Windows compiler/generated-runtime acceptance failed; inspect bounded stage logs.' }

diff --git a/tools/r62_windows_acceptance.ps1 b/tools/r62_windows_acceptance.ps1
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tools/r62_windows_acceptance.ps1
@@ -0,0 +1,134 @@
+#requires -version 5.1
+# Manual-only R62 Windows smoke acceptance. No network, elevation, or CI trigger.
+[CmdletBinding()]
+param(
+ [ValidateSet('Prepare','Audit','Screenshot')][string]$Stage='Prepare',
+ [string]$ResultsDir='',
+ [string]$LegacyCompiler='',
+ [switch]$CaptureGui
+)
+$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'
+Set-StrictMode -Version 2.0
+$root=(Resolve-Path (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')).Path
+if (-not $ResultsDir) { $ResultsDir=Join-Path $env:TEMP 'Sutram-R62-Windows-Acceptance' }
+New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ResultsDir | Out-Null
+$ResultsDir=(Resolve-Path -LiteralPath $ResultsDir).Path
+if (-not [Environment]::Is64BitOperatingSystem -or -not [Environment]::Is64BitProcess) { throw '64-bit Windows/PowerShell required.' }
+$principal=[Security.Principal.WindowsPrincipal]::new([Security.Principal.WindowsIdentity]::GetCurrent())
+if ($principal.IsInRole([Security.Principal.WindowsBuiltInRole]::Administrator)) { throw 'Use standard-user PowerShell; do not elevate.' }
+function Hash([string]$file) {
+ if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $file -PathType Leaf)) { throw "Missing file: $file" }
+ return (Get-FileHash -LiteralPath $file -Algorithm SHA256).Hash.ToLowerInvariant()
+}
+$expectedIcon='b48aeb52516433c3cce51ffe436fa04355cb938aa0b5188c60fe7c02f2923ec1'
+if ((Hash (Join-Path $root 'icons\sutram.ico')) -ne $expectedIcon) { throw 'Canonical source icon hash differs.' }
+$sample=Join-Path $ResultsDir 'R62_COLOUR_FIXTURE.sm'
+$sampleText=@'
+# GREY comment
+mukhya()
+    vitti value = 123
+    yadi (value > 100) {
+        likha("R62_SHELL_AND_RUN_OK\n")
+    }
+'@
+[IO.File]::WriteAllText($sample,$sampleText + [Environment]::NewLine,([Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)))
+function Run-Bounded([string]$exe,[string]$arguments,[string]$tag,[string]$watched='') {
+ $out=Join-Path $ResultsDir ($tag+'.stdout.txt'); $err=Join-Path $ResultsDir ($tag+'.stderr.txt')
+ $start=@{FilePath=$exe; PassThru=$true; WorkingDirectory=$root; NoNewWindow=$true; RedirectStandardOutput=$out; RedirectStandardError=$err}
+ if ($arguments) { $start.ArgumentList=$arguments }
+ $p=Start-Process @start
+ $sw=[Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew(); $oversize=$false
+ while (-not $p.HasExited -and $sw.ElapsedMilliseconds -lt 12000) {
+   if ($watched -and (Test-Path -LiteralPath $watched -PathType Leaf) -and (Get-Item -LiteralPath $watched).Length -gt 65536) { $oversize=$true; break }
+   Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 80; $p.Refresh()
+ }
+ $timed=(-not $p.HasExited)
+ if ($timed) { Stop-Process -Id $p.Id -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue; [void]$p.WaitForExit(3000) }
+ $sw.Stop(); $code=if ($timed) {-1} else {$p.ExitCode}
+ $text=if (Test-Path -LiteralPath $out) {[IO.File]::ReadAllText($out)} else {''}
+ Write-Host ("R62_NATIVE tag={0} exit={1} timeout={2} oversize={3} ms={4} stdout={5}" -f $tag,$code,$timed,$oversize,$sw.ElapsedMilliseconds,($text.Trim() -replace "[\r\n]+",' | '))
+ if ($code -ne 0 -or $oversize -or $timed) { throw "R62 $tag failed; inspect $out and $err" }
+ return $text
+}
+if ($Stage -eq 'Screenshot') {
+ if (-not $CaptureGui) { throw 'Open the fixture in the GUI, then rerun with -CaptureGui.' }
+ Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing
+ Add-Type -AssemblyName System.Windows.Forms
+ $r=[Windows.Forms.Screen]::PrimaryScreen.Bounds
+ $bmp=[Drawing.Bitmap]::new($r.Width,$r.Height)
+ $g=[Drawing.Graphics]::FromImage($bmp)
+ try { $g.CopyFromScreen($r.Location,[Drawing.Point]::Empty,$r.Size)
+       $bmp.Save((Join-Path $ResultsDir 'GUI_REVIEW_REQUIRED.png'),[Drawing.Imaging.ImageFormat]::Png) }
+ finally { $g.Dispose(); $bmp.Dispose() }
+ Write-Host 'R62_SCREENSHOT_CAPTURED; MUST visually review orange/teal/green/purple/grey, menu and shell. Screenshot is not acceptance by itself.'
+ exit 0
+}
+$cli=Join-Path $root 'win\sutram.exe'
+$gui=Join-Path $root 'sutram-ide-gui.exe'
+$setup=Join-Path $root 'windows\native-installer\output\Sutram-Setup-0.1.0-native-x64.exe'
+$installed=Join-Path $env:LOCALAPPDATA 'Programs\Sutram'
+if ($Stage -eq 'Prepare') {
+ $diag=Join-Path $root 'tools\r61_windows_compiler_diagnostics.ps1'
+ $diagArgs=@('-ResultsDir',(Join-Path $ResultsDir 'r61-native'))
+ if ($LegacyCompiler) { $diagArgs+=@('-LegacyCompiler',$LegacyCompiler) }
+ & $diag @diagArgs
+ if (-not $?) { throw 'R61 CLI diagnostics did not complete.' }
+ $nasm=(Get-Command nasm.exe -ErrorAction Stop).Source
+ $ld=(Get-Command ld.exe -ErrorAction Stop).Source
+ $obj=Join-Path $ResultsDir 'sutram-r62.obj'
+ Push-Location $root
+ try {
+   & $nasm -f win64 -dWINDOWS -I. 'src\sutram_compiler.asm' -o $obj
+   if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'NASM assembly failed.' }
+   New-Item -Path (Join-Path $root 'win') -ItemType Directory -Force | Out-Null
+   & $ld -mi386pep --entry=_start -o $cli $obj
+   if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { throw 'PE link failed.' }
+ } finally { Pop-Location }
+ & (Join-Path $root 'windows\gui\build-gui.ps1')
+ if (-not $?) { throw 'GUI build failed.' }
+ & (Join-Path $root 'windows\native-installer\build-installer.ps1')
+ if (-not $?) { throw 'Installer build failed.' }
+ [void](Run-Bounded $setup '--self-test' 'installer-self-test')
+ if ((Hash (Join-Path $root 'windows\native-installer\assets\sutram.ico')) -ne $expectedIcon) { throw 'Installer icon incorrect.' }
+ $manifest=@('R62_PREPARE_PASS',('compiler_sha256='+(Hash $cli)),('gui_sha256='+(Hash $gui)),('setup_sha256='+(Hash $setup)),('icon_sha256='+$expectedIcon),('source_sha256='+(Hash (Join-Path $root 'src\sutram_compiler.asm'))))
+ [IO.File]::WriteAllLines((Join-Path $ResultsDir 'build-manifest.txt'),$manifest,([Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false)))
+ $manifest | ForEach-Object { Write-Host $_ }
+ Write-Host "NEXT: run installer as standard user: $setup"
+ Write-Host 'After graphical wizard finishes, rerun this script with -Stage Audit.'
+ exit 0
+}
+if ($Stage -eq 'Audit') {
+ if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $installed '.sutram-install') -PathType Leaf)) { throw 'Installed marker absent.' }
+ $reg=Get-ItemProperty -LiteralPath 'HKCU:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Uninstall\Sutram' -ErrorAction Stop
+ if (-not [string]::Equals([IO.Path]::GetFullPath([string]$reg.InstallLocation).TrimEnd('\'),[IO.Path]::GetFullPath($installed).TrimEnd('\'),[StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { throw 'HKCU uninstall path invalid.' }
+ $lnk=Join-Path ([Environment]::GetFolderPath('StartMenu')) 'Programs\Sutram\Sutram IDE.lnk'
+ if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $lnk -PathType Leaf)) { throw 'Start Menu link missing.' }
+ $shell=New-Object -ComObject WScript.Shell; $sc=$shell.CreateShortcut($lnk)
+ $destGui=Join-Path $installed 'sutram-ide-gui.exe'; $icon=Join-Path $installed 'assets\sutram.ico'
+ if (-not [string]::Equals($sc.TargetPath,$destGui,[StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { throw "Shortcut target mismatch: $($sc.TargetPath)" }
+ if (-not $sc.IconLocation.StartsWith($icon,[StringComparison]::OrdinalIgnoreCase)) { throw "Shortcut icon path mismatch: $($sc.IconLocation)" }
+ if ((Hash $icon) -ne $expectedIcon) { throw 'Installed icon SHA wrong.' }
+ $destCli=Join-Path $installed 'bin\sutram.exe'
+ if ((Hash $destCli) -ne (Hash $cli)) { throw 'Packaged/installed compiler does not match tested current compiler.' }
+ $log=Join-Path $installed 'install.log'
+ if (-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $log -PathType Leaf)) { throw 'Successful installer log missing; inspect original wizard failure log under TEMP\Sutram-Setup-*.' }
+ $actualLog=[IO.File]::ReadAllText($log)
+ Copy-Item -LiteralPath $log -Destination (Join-Path $ResultsDir 'observed-install.log') -Force
+ if ($actualLog -notmatch 'Installation complete:' -or $actualLog -match 'ERROR:') { throw 'Installer log does not prove successful completion.' }
+ Write-Host "R62_INSTALL_LOG_INSPECTED $log"
+ $generated=Join-Path $ResultsDir 'r62_installed_hello.exe'
+ [void](Run-Bounded $destCli ('"'+$sample+'" "'+$generated+'"') 'installed-compile' $generated)
+ if ((Get-Item -LiteralPath $generated).Length -gt 65536) { throw 'Oversized generated PE.' }
+ $stdout=Run-Bounded $generated '' 'installed-program'
+ if ($stdout.Trim() -ne 'R62_SHELL_AND_RUN_OK') { throw "Wrong native stdout: $stdout" }
+ $p=Start-Process -FilePath $destGui -WorkingDirectory $installed -PassThru
+ $seen=$false
+ for ($i=0;$i -lt 40;$i++) {
+   Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 250; $p.Refresh()
+   if ($p.HasExited) { throw "Installed GUI exited: $($p.ExitCode)" }
+   if ($p.MainWindowHandle -ne [IntPtr]::Zero) { $seen=$true; break }
+ }
+ if (-not $seen) { throw 'Installed GUI failed to create a visible main window.' }
+ Write-Host 'R62_AUDIT_PASS: HKCU, real install log, shortcut, exact canonical ICO, byte-matched compiler, native stdout, GUI window.'
+ Write-Host "MANUAL: in installed GUI File > Open $sample; test editor Run and >>> shell, inspect five colours; capture via -Stage Screenshot -CaptureGui."
+}
\ No newline at end of file

diff --git a/windows/native-installer/install-core.ps1 b/windows/native-installer/install-core.ps1
--- a/windows/native-installer/install-core.ps1
+++ b/windows/native-installer/install-core.ps1
@@ -13,6 +13,36 @@ function Log([string]$Message) {
     $stamp = [DateTime]::Now.ToString('yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss')
     Add-Content -LiteralPath $LogPath -Value ("[{0}] {1}" -f $stamp,$Message) -Encoding UTF8
 }
+# No unbounded compiler preflights: a broken native compiler must not
+# freeze the Windows wizard forever inside WaitForSingleObject(INFINITE).
+# Keep the log in the user's TEMP directory and fail closed (no install).
+function Invoke-SutramSelfTest([string]$ExePath,[string]$Argument,[string]$Stage) {
+    $p = New-Object System.Diagnostics.Process
+    $p.StartInfo.FileName = $ExePath
+    $p.StartInfo.Arguments = $Argument
+    $p.StartInfo.UseShellExecute = $false
+    $p.StartInfo.RedirectStandardOutput = $true
+    $p.StartInfo.RedirectStandardError = $true
+    $p.StartInfo.CreateNoWindow = $true
+    try {
+        Log ("Native self-test start: " + $Stage)
+        if (-not $p.Start()) { throw ("Unable to start " + $Stage) }
+        if (-not $p.WaitForExit(8000)) {
+            try { $p.Kill() } catch {}
+            try { [void]$p.WaitForExit(2000) } catch {}
+            throw ("Native compiler timed out during " + $Stage + " after 8000 ms; installation aborted.")
+        }
